>> title: Hot Water Cornbread
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: cornmeal, southern, fried, skillet
>> counters: Meat and Three, Smokehouse
>> aka: fried cornbread, corn cakes, hot water corn bread
>> servings: 8
>> time: 30 min
>> pairs-with: hoppin-john, dirty-rice
>> step.2: scald to a stiff mush, rest 10 min
>> step.3: loosen with buttermilk to a spoonable batter
>> step.4: heat in a cast-iron skillet to 350°F (175°C)
>> step.5: fry in the hot fat, 3-in cakes, 3 min per side

Whisk @fine white cornmeal{2%cup}(270 g), @fine sea salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g), @sugar{1%tsp}(4 g).

Scald @&(~1)seasoned meal{} with @boiling water{1 3/4%cup}(420 mL), @bacon fat{2%Tbsp}(25 g), stirring to a stiff mush, then rest ~rest{10%min}.

Loosen @&(~1)scalded meal{} with @buttermilk{1/4%cup}(60 mL) to a thick spoonable batter.

Heat @bacon drippings for frying{1/2%cup}(120 mL) in a #10-in cast-iron skillet{} to 350°F (175°C).

Spoon @&(~2)batter{} into @&(~1)hot fat{} as flattened 3-in cakes and fry ~fry{3%min} per side.
